From: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
Subject: serial: base: preserve console TX on hangup for opt-in ports

When procd's askconsole fork calls TIOCSCTTY with force=1 the kernel
hangs up the previous session, which triggers uart_hangup() ->
uart_shutdown() -> serial_base_port_shutdown() ->
serial_base_port_set_tx(false). Stopping TX silences all subsequent
kernel console output permanently.

Add an opt-in DT boolean property "keep-console-tx-on-hangup" that
suppresses the TX-disable in serial_base_port_shutdown(). This keeps
the change strictly per-device: no other platform or port type is
affected unless they add the property.

The EN751627 UART node sets this property because procd runs on that
platform and the UART is always the system console.

Signed-off-by: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_port.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_port.c
@@ -109,6 +109,17 @@ void serial_base_port_startup(struct uart_port *port)
 void serial_base_port_shutdown(struct uart_port *port)
 {
 	struct serial_port_device *port_dev = port->port_dev;
+	/*
+	 * If the device node opts in with "keep-console-tx-on-hangup",
+	 * do not disable TX on shutdown. This covers platforms (e.g.
+	 * EN751627) where procd askconsole calls TIOCSCTTY with force=1,
+	 * triggering uart_hangup() -> uart_shutdown() -> here, which
+	 * permanently silences the console. The property is opt-in so
+	 * no other platform is affected.
+	 */
+	if (port->dev &&
+	    device_property_read_bool(port->dev, "keep-console-tx-on-hangup"))
+		return;

 	serial_base_port_set_tx(port, port_dev, false);
 }
